Source licences and required attribution statements
---------------------------------------------------
The records come from three official registries. Each keeps its own licence, and
the statements below must travel with any reuse of the data.

France. Source: Ministere de l'Education nationale, Direction du numerique pour
l'education, "Annuaire de l'education" (dataset fr-en-annuaire-education),
data.education.gouv.fr, published under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence
version 2.0 (Etalab), https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/
Data downloaded on 2026-11-17 (registry last update 2026-11-17).

England and Wales. Source: Department for Education, "Get Information About
Schools" (GIAS) establishment data, https://get-information-schools.service.gov.uk/
Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0,
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
Data downloaded on 2026-11-17.

The Netherlands. Source: DUO (Dienst Uitvoering Onderwijs), Open Onderwijsdata,
school locations of primary and secondary education,
https://duo.nl/open_onderwijsdata/ , released under CC0 1.0 Universal.
Data downloaded on 2026-11-17. Credit is given as a courtesy.

This dataset is a selection and re-formatting of those records (schools whose
official name contains "Montessori"), with the summaries and links added by
Montessori Theory. It is not an official product of any of the three bodies and
they do not endorse it. Contact details of schools (telephone, email, head
teacher names) are not included.
